---
#1697: `BagState` is the name agent `Bag`'s handlers give its state record (its
`Cell` fields), so a type of that name would be silently replaced there. It's
rejected rather than renamed: unlike the compiler's other derived names, a
program can write this one.
---
context demo.c

type BagState = { label: String }

agent Bag {
  key id: String
  store n: Cell[Int]

  on call add(k: Int) -> Effect[Int] { k }
}
